# Content Style & Copywriting Standards

All user-visible copy must read like it was written by an expert human copywriter for retail and business owners, never like machine or AI output.

## Invariant Rules

- **Banned Characters (CRITICAL)**: NEVER use em-dash (`—`, U+2014), en-dash (`–`, U+2013), or arrows (`→`, U+2192) in any user-visible string (`messages/*.json`, `content/docs/**`, JSON-LD descriptions, route outputs like `llms.txt`, or `.tsx` rendered text).
- **No Dash Substitutions**: Do NOT substitute banned dashes with `--` or a floating hyphen ` - `. Use hyphens ONLY inside compound words (`end-of-day`, `low-stock`, `sign-up`).
- **Receipt Mono Annotations**: Use a middle dot (`·`) with zero-padded chapter labels: `NO. 01 · THE PROBLEM` / `رقم 01 · المشكلة`.
- **Comparison Table Markers**: Use `[✓]` for included and `[✗]` for excluded — NEVER use `[—]`.
- **Docs Navigation Paths**: Use bold with `>` separator: `**Settings > Branding**`, NEVER arrows.
- **Docs Status Transitions**: Use prose transitions: `"Pending, then Preparing, then Ready"` or `"Pending to Ready"`.
- **Banned SaaS Buzzwords**: Avoid generic AI filler: `unlock`, `empower`, `seamless`, `revolutionize`, `comprehensive`, `game-changer`.

## ❌ FORBIDDEN vs ✅ REQUIRED

### 1. Punctuation & Connectors

```text
// ❌ FORBIDDEN
Free forever plan — no credit card needed
Six ready reports — overview, profit, customers
Track stock in real time — never oversell again
Pending → Approved → Completed
Settings → Branding → Logo

// ✅ REQUIRED
Free forever plan, no credit card needed
Six ready reports: overview, profit, customers
Track stock in real time. Never oversell again.
Pending, then Approved, then Completed
Settings > Branding > Logo
```

### 2. Eyebrow Annotations & Ledger Slips

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN
eyebrow="NO. 01 — WHAT YOU GET"
<td>[—] Not Included</td>

// ✅ REQUIRED
eyebrow={`${tLedger('no')} 01 · ${t('features.badge')}`} // Renders: NO. 01 · WHAT YOU GET
<td>[✗] Not Included</td>
```

### 3. Voice & Persona

- **Direct & Merchant-Practical**: Speak directly to one shop owner (`"Run your shop"`, `"Track stock on your phone"`).
- **Concrete over Abstract**: Focus on tangible features (barcode scanner, thermal receipts, inventory alerts, WhatsApp orders).
- **Honest Claims Only**: Only claim shipped capabilities; no exaggerated stats, fake testimonials, or trial tricks.
- **Arabic Register**: Modern Standard Arabic with light Egyptian merchant flavor (`شوف`, `اللي`, `مش`, `عندك`). Never machine-translate literally from English.
- **English Brand/Technical Terms in Arabic**: Keep acronyms and names as English: `Cashvio`, `POS`, `USB`, `QR`, `CSV`, `PDF`, `PNG`.
